  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Riemann Sums and Definite Integrals: Calculations and Limits.</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the definite integral \(\displaystyle \int_{@aa@}^{@bb@}{@func@} dx\)</p>
<br>
<p> Compute the following and fill in the blanks.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \Delta x = \frac{b-a}{n} \implies \Delta x = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:12px">\(\displaystyle x_j = a+ j\Delta x \implies x_j = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle f(x_j) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<br>
<p>\(\displaystyle \sum_j ^n  f(x_j) \Delta x = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]] </p>
<br>
<p>Evaluate the integral .</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{{n \to \infty}} \sum_j ^n  f(x_j) \Delta x = \) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]] </p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>Given that \(\displaystyle \int_a^b f(x) = \lim_{{n \to \infty}} \sum_j ^n  f(x_j) \Delta x  \)</p>

<p>Let us go ahead and evaluate this integral \(\displaystyle \int_{@aa@}^{@bb@}{@func@}\); </p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \Delta x = \frac{b-a}{n} \implies \Delta x = {@ta1@} \) </p>
<p style="margin-bottom:12px">\(\displaystyle x_j = a+ j\Delta x \implies x_j = {@ta2@}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle f(x_j) = {@ta3@}\) </p>
<p>\( \displaystyle f(x_j) \Delta x = {@f_xj@}\)</p>

<br>
<p>Now we go ahead and compute \(\displaystyle \sum_j ^n  f(x_j)\)</p>

<p>We need to substitute the following when setting up the Reimann sum:</p>
<p> \(\displaystyle \sum_j ^n j^2 = \frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}\) and \(\displaystyle  \sum_j ^n j = \frac{n(n+1)}{n}\), we can go ahead and form the Reimann sum as shown,</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle \sum_j ^n  f(x_j) \Delta x = {@coef_j2@}\left( {@sum_j2@} \right ) + {@coef_j@}\left( {@sum_j@} \right )+{@coef_j0@} = {@ta4@}\) </p>


<br>
<p>Finally,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \lim_{{n \to \infty}} \sum_j ^n  f(x_j) \Delta x  \implies \lim_{{n \to \infty}} {@ta4@} = {@ta5@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
